{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzy34SYFBViUiMrVTvvd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**What's required:** manager approval before the purchase, and a notice to finance within 24 hours after it. Advance finance approval is waived.\n\n**Why:**\n\n1. **It qualifies as an emergency (DEF-1).** The purchase addresses \"an immediate operational… risk that cannot reasonably await normal approval.\" That matches the definition, so this is more than just calling it \"urgent\" (EMG-3).\n\n2. **The normal rule would require finance approval.** The purchase is on October 12, 2026, which is after July 1, 2025, so the $2,500 limit applies (AMD-2). $4,000 is above that limit, so ordinarily both manager and finance approval would be needed (EXP-2).\n\n3. **The emergency exception applies (EMG-1).** The purchase is $5,000 or less, the vendor is approved, and the emergency qualifies. That removes the advance finance approval, but:\n   - **Manager approval is still required before the purchase** (EMG-1, EXP-3, EMG-3).\n   - **Finance must be notified within 24 hours after the purchase** (EMG-1). This is only a notice, not an approval (DEF-2).\n\n**Not required:**\n- **Travel-office approval:** this isn't airfare (TRV-1).\n- **Compliance-officer authorization:** that's only needed for a prohibited vendor, and this vendor is approved (VEN-1/VEN-2).\n\n**Timing:** Today is October 13, 2026, so the 24-hour window to notify finance runs out today, at the same time of day the purchase was made on October 12. If finance hasn't been told yet, that should happen now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2473,"cache_read_input_tokens":5592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2473},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagn